explained\">Help</span></nav>\n</aside>\n<div id=\"w-twbox-intro\">\n<div id=\"w-object-profile\">\n<div id=\"w-twbox-image\"><img alt=\"latest?cb=20080619201951&amp;path-prefix=en&amp;format=original\" class=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Wand_of_Draconia_f8322f.gif\"/></div>\n<div id=\"w-twbox-look\"><div class=\"item-look tibiatext tibiagreen\">You see a wand of draconia.<br/>Imbuements: (Empty Slot, Empty Slot).<br/>Classification: 1 Tier: 0.<div class=\"p-reqs\">It can only be wielded properly by sorcerers of level 22 or higher.<br/></div><div class=\"p-weight\">It weighs 27.00 oz.</div><div class=\"p-flavortext\">This wand holds the spirit and soul of a dragon lord.</div><br/></div></div>\n<div class=\"\" id=\"w-twbox-sounds\"></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:left;\"></div>\n<div id=\"w-object-notes\">\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-Notes\">Notes</span></h3>\n<p>The <a href=\"#/wiki/Sorcerer\">sorcerer</a>'s equivalent of the <a href=\"#/wiki/Druid\">druid</a>'s Northwind Rod and the <a href=\"#/wiki/Fire%20Damage\">fire damage</a> counterpart to the <a href=\"#/wiki/Wand%20of%20Decay\">Wand of Decay</a>, which typically makes it more valuable, as, at a lower level, fire is a more useful element than death.\n</p>\n</div>\n<div id=\"w-object-proficiency\">\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"w-Weapon_Proficiency\">Weapon Proficiency</span></h3>\n<div class=\"weapon_proficiency weapon_proficiency_border\">\n<table class=\"weapon_proficiency_number_table\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>4\n</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<table class=\"weapon_proficiency_table\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><div class=\"weapon_proficiency_block weapon_proficiency_border\"><div><div class=\"weapon_proficiency_icon\" title=\"Life Gain on Kill\">\n<div></div>\n<div><img alt=\"latest?cb=20250625211543&amp;path-prefix=en\" class=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"assets/wiki/Weapon_Proficiency_Border_Active_417a88.png\"/></div>\n<div class=\"img32\">